To skip the rest of the router's middleware functions, call `next('router')`
to pass control back out of the router instance.

Dieses Beispiel zeigt einen Middleware-Sub-Stack an, der GET-Anfragen im `/user/:id`-Pfad behandelt.

```cjs title="index.cjs"
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const router = express.Router();

// predicate the router with a check and bail out when needed
router.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (!req.headers['x-auth']) return next('router');
  next();
});

router.get('/user/:id', (req, res) => {
  res.send('hello, user!');
});

// use the router and 401 anything falling through
app.use('/admin', router, (req, res) => {
  res.sendStatus(401);
});
```

